      {
        "id": 229924,
        "name": "catDreaming",
        "username": "catDreaming",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/4491bb/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-03-06T23:08:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I ardently disagree. While it does help for heroes to have multi targeting attacks, I've had players absolutely mow down some of the villains I've thrown at them, even with defensive abilities. Heroes can do a lot more damage together, and often have more incentive to work together than villains do.<br>\n<br>\nEdit: Just pulled up my excel spreadsheet for calculating average dice pool results, and a bit of quick math.<br>\nd6/d6/d6 dice pool has an average mid of 3. So, 3 damage. 3 damage*4 heroes is 12 damage per round. Over 8 rounds, that's an average of 96 damage, which is enough to take down one of those villains and drop a second to about half. That's no abilities, just a d6/d6/d6 mid die attack.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:04:47.842Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
