      {
        "id": 229928,
        "name": "mistergone",
        "username": "mistergone",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mistergone/{size}/1898_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-03-07T00:11:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>\"Variety\" just means that, sometimes, players have abilities that focus on Minions or Environments or Overcomes, and an all-Villain fight might leave out&nbsp;some of their abilities. And remember that Hero Points come from Overcome actions (because of Principles), and Challenges are the main way those come into play. Of course, you can always give out Hero Points in another way :-)</p>\n<p>If you have a team of 4 Villains and you want them all to play together, it's possible to have them all but change up how they work mechanically in the fight. For instance, assuming you have 4 Heroes:</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>One of the Villains isn't fighting, but is causing a different problem! (3 Villains, and a Challenge based on the 4th Villain.)</li>\n\t<li>Two of the Villains aren't as tough as the others. (2 Villains, 2 Lieutenants, and then you have space for a Challenge or Environment)</li>\n\t<li>One of the Villains is threatening civilians, damaging bridges, creating gas leaks (3 Villains, and an Environment based on what the 4th Villain is doing.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If the Villain is creating a Challenge or an Environment-equivalent element, you can always have their character sheet if the players Attack them, and skip their \"Actions\" in favor of describing the ongoing effects Challenge or the Environment effects. If they take out all the Villain's HP, that might \"defeat the Villain,\" but there might be consequences because they didn't deal with the Challenge or Environment.</p>\n<p>Of course, I think we can assume your scenes aren't&nbsp;<strong>ALL</strong>&nbsp;going to be 4 Villains, and if you do run a 4 Villain scene every once in a while, it's not the end of the world. Still, I always like to think outside the box, so thinking about how to run \"4 Villains\" but do it in mechanically unique ways was a fun exercise for me. :-)</p>",
        "post_number": 8,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:04:48.134Z",
